[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186157305 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" "question-727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157303 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" "question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" :question/id #uuid "8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-84826" :question/problem "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(-3,-2)$ and which passes through the point $(2,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-3,-2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+3=2pt,\\,y+2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(2,3),$ we can substitute $x=2$ and $y=3$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5=2pt \\\\ 5=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =2pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{5}{2p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =p{(\\frac{5}{2p})}^{2} \\\\ 5 & =p\\cdot \\frac{25}{4{p}^{2}} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{25}{4p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+3=2(\\frac{5}{4})t,\\,y+2=(\\frac{5}{4}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+3=\\frac{5}{2}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{5}{4}{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/id #uuid "46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4" "answer-606af933-7d01-5aba-a01d-1698e07eb2f5" "answer-5fd94bab-ba3d-53e6-b7a3-be9c9c7e8fa8" "answer-e06459cd-3712-586f-bc68-69909dacd4dd" "answer-9bd7ca21-f69d-5100-a76d-a62b09fb4809"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4" :answer/id #uuid "481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=\\frac{5}{2}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{5}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-606af933-7d01-5aba-a01d-1698e07eb2f5" :answer/id #uuid "606af933-7d01-5aba-a01d-1698e07eb2f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=\\frac{8}{5}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{4}{5}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fd94bab-ba3d-53e6-b7a3-be9c9c7e8fa8" :answer/id #uuid "5fd94bab-ba3d-53e6-b7a3-be9c9c7e8fa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=\\frac{5}{2}t,\\,y-3=\\frac{5}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e06459cd-3712-586f-bc68-69909dacd4dd" :answer/id #uuid "e06459cd-3712-586f-bc68-69909dacd4dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2=\\frac{5}{4}t,\\,y-3=\\frac{5}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bd7ca21-f69d-5100-a76d-a62b09fb4809" :answer/id #uuid "9bd7ca21-f69d-5100-a76d-a62b09fb4809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=\\frac{8}{5}t,\\,y-2=\\frac{4}{5}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66" :question/id #uuid "4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66" :question/math-academy-id "q-106451" :question/problem "![](images/96/96e1647f6069dee4219f8cb92e3fb4277396394c016b27ecd4de557f87257000.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(3,-2),$ and passes through the point $(7,-6).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(3,-2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-3=2pt,\\,y+2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(7,-6),$ we can substitute $x=7$ and $y=-6$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4=2pt \\\\ -4=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-3=2(-1)t,\\,y+2=(-1){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-3=-2t,\\,y+2=-{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/id #uuid "829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e778123-9ee0-54cc-9eb6-f27d0cb7ddbf" "answer-aa4dd6aa-918f-5eba-ab69-561c4e51cffe" "answer-1d828ed6-02a5-556a-bcf0-6de2c7929742" "answer-cbac0851-5569-524e-ac10-92470ba43d20" "answer-c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e778123-9ee0-54cc-9eb6-f27d0cb7ddbf" :answer/id #uuid "9e778123-9ee0-54cc-9eb6-f27d0cb7ddbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=-2t,\\,\\,y+2=-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa4dd6aa-918f-5eba-ab69-561c4e51cffe" :answer/id #uuid "aa4dd6aa-918f-5eba-ab69-561c4e51cffe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=-2t,\\,\\,y-2=-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d828ed6-02a5-556a-bcf0-6de2c7929742" :answer/id #uuid "1d828ed6-02a5-556a-bcf0-6de2c7929742" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=-t,\\,\\,y+2=-2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbac0851-5569-524e-ac10-92470ba43d20" :answer/id #uuid "cbac0851-5569-524e-ac10-92470ba43d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=-2t,\\,\\,y+2=-2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05" :answer/id #uuid "c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3=-2t,\\,\\,y+2=-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" :question/id #uuid "13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-106506" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx+1=2{t}^{2},\\,y+3=4t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x+1}{2},\\,t=\\frac{y+3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{y+3}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{x+1}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{x+1}{2} \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =16\\cdot (\\frac{x+1}{2}) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =8(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/id #uuid "314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c5d3114-e499-590c-baf7-861605384f54" "answer-2e072a8a-4c4e-573b-8869-941c8567a11b" "answer-7a134ec0-3a05-56eb-ad2c-0e83ebd565ee" "answer-dc78eb36-9d33-50e7-9b6c-c918281f4ed5" "answer-6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c5d3114-e499-590c-baf7-861605384f54" :answer/id #uuid "7c5d3114-e499-590c-baf7-861605384f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=4(y+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e072a8a-4c4e-573b-8869-941c8567a11b" :answer/id #uuid "2e072a8a-4c4e-573b-8869-941c8567a11b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=8(y+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a134ec0-3a05-56eb-ad2c-0e83ebd565ee" :answer/id #uuid "7a134ec0-3a05-56eb-ad2c-0e83ebd565ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=-8(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc78eb36-9d33-50e7-9b6c-c918281f4ed5" :answer/id #uuid "dc78eb36-9d33-50e7-9b6c-c918281f4ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=4(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6" :answer/id #uuid "6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=8(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0" :question/id #uuid "727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-84849" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx-4=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =2(x-4),\\,t=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =(y+1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=2(x-4)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =2(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d" :answer-field/id #uuid "44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306" :answer-field/choices ["answer-830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306" "answer-c1fc5336-dfe4-5a79-95c6-2401457bbad9" "answer-81396d4d-0bd7-575b-b2e7-739740b6660c" "answer-bce99d0a-b922-5732-8a5d-54c719314068" "answer-761e2e34-2b73-575e-ad93-69b3ef7a4509"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306" :answer/id #uuid "830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=2(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1fc5336-dfe4-5a79-95c6-2401457bbad9" :answer/id #uuid "c1fc5336-dfe4-5a79-95c6-2401457bbad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=8(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81396d4d-0bd7-575b-b2e7-739740b6660c" :answer/id #uuid "81396d4d-0bd7-575b-b2e7-739740b6660c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bce99d0a-b922-5732-8a5d-54c719314068" :answer/id #uuid "bce99d0a-b922-5732-8a5d-54c719314068" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=2(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-761e2e34-2b73-575e-ad93-69b3ef7a4509" :answer/id #uuid "761e2e34-2b73-575e-ad93-69b3ef7a4509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=8(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" :question/id #uuid "8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3"] ["question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-84826"] ["question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" :question/problem "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(-3,-2)$ and which passes through the point $(2,3)?$"] ["question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-3,-2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+3=2pt,\\,y+2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(2,3),$ we can substitute $x=2$ and $y=3$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5=2pt \\\\ 5=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =2pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{5}{2p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =p{(\\frac{5}{2p})}^{2} \\\\ 5 & =p\\cdot \\frac{25}{4{p}^{2}} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{25}{4p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+3=2(\\frac{5}{4})t,\\,y+2=(\\frac{5}{4}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+3=\\frac{5}{2}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{5}{4}{t}^{2}.\n$$"] ["question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/id #uuid "46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e"] ["answer-481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4" :answer/id #uuid "481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4"] ["answer-481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4" :answer/value "x+3=\\frac{5}{2}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{5}{4}{t}^{2}"] ["answer-606af933-7d01-5aba-a01d-1698e07eb2f5" :answer/id #uuid "606af933-7d01-5aba-a01d-1698e07eb2f5"] ["answer-606af933-7d01-5aba-a01d-1698e07eb2f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-606af933-7d01-5aba-a01d-1698e07eb2f5" :answer/value "x+3=\\frac{8}{5}t,\\,y+2=\\frac{4}{5}{t}^{2}"] ["answer-5fd94bab-ba3d-53e6-b7a3-be9c9c7e8fa8" :answer/id #uuid "5fd94bab-ba3d-53e6-b7a3-be9c9c7e8fa8"] ["answer-5fd94bab-ba3d-53e6-b7a3-be9c9c7e8fa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5fd94bab-ba3d-53e6-b7a3-be9c9c7e8fa8" :answer/value "x-2=\\frac{5}{2}t,\\,y-3=\\frac{5}{4}{t}^{2}"] ["answer-e06459cd-3712-586f-bc68-69909dacd4dd" :answer/id #uuid "e06459cd-3712-586f-bc68-69909dacd4dd"] ["answer-e06459cd-3712-586f-bc68-69909dacd4dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e06459cd-3712-586f-bc68-69909dacd4dd" :answer/value "x-2=\\frac{5}{4}t,\\,y-3=\\frac{5}{4}{t}^{2}"] ["answer-9bd7ca21-f69d-5100-a76d-a62b09fb4809" :answer/id #uuid "9bd7ca21-f69d-5100-a76d-a62b09fb4809"] ["answer-9bd7ca21-f69d-5100-a76d-a62b09fb4809" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9bd7ca21-f69d-5100-a76d-a62b09fb4809" :answer/value "x-3=\\frac{8}{5}t,\\,y-2=\\frac{4}{5}{t}^{2}"] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/correct "answer-481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4"] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-481610f4-96eb-5391-8fa0-5b8e3917e1a4"] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-606af933-7d01-5aba-a01d-1698e07eb2f5"] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-5fd94bab-ba3d-53e6-b7a3-be9c9c7e8fa8"] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-e06459cd-3712-586f-bc68-69909dacd4dd"] ["answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-9bd7ca21-f69d-5100-a76d-a62b09fb4809"] ["question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-46647a5c-2b95-53fe-940a-e6b35e9ddd8e"] [17592186157303 :knowledge-point/questions "question-8ba3cd0d-7f42-50d0-93f6-108a716173e3"] ["question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66" :question/id #uuid "4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66"] ["question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66" :question/math-academy-id "q-106451"] ["question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66" :question/problem "![](images/96/96e1647f6069dee4219f8cb92e3fb4277396394c016b27ecd4de557f87257000.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?"] ["question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(3,-2),$ and passes through the point $(7,-6).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(3,-2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-3=2pt,\\,y+2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(7,-6),$ we can substitute $x=7$ and $y=-6$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4=2pt \\\\ -4=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-3=2(-1)t,\\,y+2=(-1){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-3=-2t,\\,y+2=-{t}^{2}.\n$$"] ["question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/id #uuid "829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780"] ["answer-9e778123-9ee0-54cc-9eb6-f27d0cb7ddbf" :answer/id #uuid "9e778123-9ee0-54cc-9eb6-f27d0cb7ddbf"] ["answer-9e778123-9ee0-54cc-9eb6-f27d0cb7ddbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9e778123-9ee0-54cc-9eb6-f27d0cb7ddbf" :answer/value "x+3=-2t,\\,\\,y+2=-{t}^{2}"] ["answer-aa4dd6aa-918f-5eba-ab69-561c4e51cffe" :answer/id #uuid "aa4dd6aa-918f-5eba-ab69-561c4e51cffe"] ["answer-aa4dd6aa-918f-5eba-ab69-561c4e51cffe" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-aa4dd6aa-918f-5eba-ab69-561c4e51cffe" :answer/value "x+3=-2t,\\,\\,y-2=-{t}^{2}"] ["answer-1d828ed6-02a5-556a-bcf0-6de2c7929742" :answer/id #uuid "1d828ed6-02a5-556a-bcf0-6de2c7929742"] ["answer-1d828ed6-02a5-556a-bcf0-6de2c7929742" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1d828ed6-02a5-556a-bcf0-6de2c7929742" :answer/value "x+3=-t,\\,\\,y+2=-2{t}^{2}"] ["answer-cbac0851-5569-524e-ac10-92470ba43d20" :answer/id #uuid "cbac0851-5569-524e-ac10-92470ba43d20"] ["answer-cbac0851-5569-524e-ac10-92470ba43d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cbac0851-5569-524e-ac10-92470ba43d20" :answer/value "x-3=-2t,\\,\\,y+2=-2{t}^{2}"] ["answer-c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05" :answer/id #uuid "c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05"] ["answer-c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05" :answer/value "x-3=-2t,\\,\\,y+2=-{t}^{2}"] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/correct "answer-c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05"] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/choices "answer-9e778123-9ee0-54cc-9eb6-f27d0cb7ddbf"] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/choices "answer-aa4dd6aa-918f-5eba-ab69-561c4e51cffe"] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/choices "answer-1d828ed6-02a5-556a-bcf0-6de2c7929742"] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/choices "answer-cbac0851-5569-524e-ac10-92470ba43d20"] ["answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780" :answer-field/choices "answer-c0ba1921-c107-5fe6-bfe7-38c56ef94a05"] ["question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-829f2828-1700-5400-9439-0d028651d780"] [17592186157303 :knowledge-point/questions "question-4e648a6d-37fa-5da0-b09f-42f9d00baf66"] ["question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" :question/id #uuid "13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc"] ["question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-106506"] ["question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx+1=2{t}^{2},\\,y+3=4t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"] ["question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x+1}{2},\\,t=\\frac{y+3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{y+3}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{x+1}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{x+1}{2} \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =16\\cdot (\\frac{x+1}{2}) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =8(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/id #uuid "314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86"] ["answer-7c5d3114-e499-590c-baf7-861605384f54" :answer/id #uuid "7c5d3114-e499-590c-baf7-861605384f54"] ["answer-7c5d3114-e499-590c-baf7-861605384f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7c5d3114-e499-590c-baf7-861605384f54" :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=4(y+3)"] ["answer-2e072a8a-4c4e-573b-8869-941c8567a11b" :answer/id #uuid "2e072a8a-4c4e-573b-8869-941c8567a11b"] ["answer-2e072a8a-4c4e-573b-8869-941c8567a11b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2e072a8a-4c4e-573b-8869-941c8567a11b" :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=8(y+3)"] ["answer-7a134ec0-3a05-56eb-ad2c-0e83ebd565ee" :answer/id #uuid "7a134ec0-3a05-56eb-ad2c-0e83ebd565ee"] ["answer-7a134ec0-3a05-56eb-ad2c-0e83ebd565ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7a134ec0-3a05-56eb-ad2c-0e83ebd565ee" :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=-8(x+1)"] ["answer-dc78eb36-9d33-50e7-9b6c-c918281f4ed5" :answer/id #uuid "dc78eb36-9d33-50e7-9b6c-c918281f4ed5"] ["answer-dc78eb36-9d33-50e7-9b6c-c918281f4ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dc78eb36-9d33-50e7-9b6c-c918281f4ed5" :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=4(x+1)"] ["answer-6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6" :answer/id #uuid "6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6"] ["answer-6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6" :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=8(x+1)"] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/correct "answer-6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6"] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/choices "answer-7c5d3114-e499-590c-baf7-861605384f54"] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/choices "answer-2e072a8a-4c4e-573b-8869-941c8567a11b"] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/choices "answer-7a134ec0-3a05-56eb-ad2c-0e83ebd565ee"] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/choices "answer-dc78eb36-9d33-50e7-9b6c-c918281f4ed5"] ["answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86" :answer-field/choices "answer-6e7f9396-d71d-5308-95cc-a34867a20ca6"] ["question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-314ab3a0-11b2-5836-a9a6-779f4e2cfc86"] [17592186157305 :knowledge-point/questions "question-13a87bfd-ec89-5321-9298-2cba42bc0bbc"] ["question-727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0" :question/id #uuid "727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0"] ["question-727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-84849"] ["question-727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx-4=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"] ["question-727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =2(x-4),\\,t=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =(y+1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=2(x-4)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =2(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-727c8803-de94-5b7f-a91c-cc70ef9900c0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d" :answer-field/id #uuid "44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d"] ["answer-830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306" :answer/id #uuid "830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306"] ["answer-830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306" :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=2(x-4)"] ["answer-c1fc5336-dfe4-5a79-95c6-2401457bbad9" :answer/id #uuid "c1fc5336-dfe4-5a79-95c6-2401457bbad9"] ["answer-c1fc5336-dfe4-5a79-95c6-2401457bbad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c1fc5336-dfe4-5a79-95c6-2401457bbad9" :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=8(x-4)"] ["answer-81396d4d-0bd7-575b-b2e7-739740b6660c" :answer/id #uuid "81396d4d-0bd7-575b-b2e7-739740b6660c"] ["answer-81396d4d-0bd7-575b-b2e7-739740b6660c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-81396d4d-0bd7-575b-b2e7-739740b6660c" :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}(x-4)"] ["answer-bce99d0a-b922-5732-8a5d-54c719314068" :answer/id #uuid "bce99d0a-b922-5732-8a5d-54c719314068"] ["answer-bce99d0a-b922-5732-8a5d-54c719314068" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bce99d0a-b922-5732-8a5d-54c719314068" :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=2(x+4)"] ["answer-761e2e34-2b73-575e-ad93-69b3ef7a4509" :answer/id #uuid "761e2e34-2b73-575e-ad93-69b3ef7a4509"] ["answer-761e2e34-2b73-575e-ad93-69b3ef7a4509" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-761e2e34-2b73-575e-ad93-69b3ef7a4509" :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=8(x+4)"] ["answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d" :answer-field/correct "answer-830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306"] ["answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d" :answer-field/choices "answer-830c8b4f-dd15-5945-be2a-c16066461306"] ["answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a60-9d70-6fd1640a128d" :answer-field/choices "answer-c1fc5336-dfe4-5a79-95c6-2401457bbad9"] ["answer-field-44ae7850-0329-5a